From 0282b36b8985f0e823c569918f64a834f7720b22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:16:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the power menu names its two restarts by what they
 do

"Restart LibreELEC Hades" restarted only the interface (RestartApp(),
added by Hades because Quit is hidden on LibreELEC) and read as a restart
of the whole system, while "Reboot" restarted the PC, which comes back to
this system (BootNext). The first was easily taken
for the second. Now:

- Reset(): "Restart LibreELEC Hades" (Estuary #54304, in place of the
  core's "Reboot");
- RestartApp(): "Restart the interface" (#52501);
- "Restart into Windows" as it was.

In English, and in Spanish of Spain, Argentina and Mexico.
